## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design per-tenant secrets strategy, runtime access flow, rotation, and CI safety beyond data isolation.

## Key Concepts
- Secrets Manager per-tenant isolation
- Workload Identity for runtime retrieval
- CMEK-backed encryption and rotation
- CI gate validating cross-tenant access and rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
const {SecretManagerServiceClient} = require('@google-cloud/secret-manager');
const client = new SecretManagerServiceClient();
async function accessSecret(tenantId, suffix) {
  const name = `projects/${PROJECT_ID}/secrets/tenant-${tenantId}-${suffix}/versions/latest`;
  const [version] = await client.accessSecretVersion({name});
  return version.payload.data.toString('utf8');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test rotation impact on live traffic?
- How would you revoke access for a suspended tenant?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical, end-to-end thinking for data lifecycle and cross-service cleanup in a real GCP setup.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant-based data tagging and discovery across services
- Safe deletion strategies and audit trail
- Backup scrub/retention implications with CMEK
- IAM least privilege and cross-service permissions
- Validation and rollback planning

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-deletion snippet (conceptual only)
async function purgeTenant(tenantId){
  await revokeTenantAccess(tenantId);
  await purgeCloudSql(tenantId);
  await deleteCloudStoragePrefix(tenantId);
  await deleteFirestoreDocs(tenantId);
  await purgePubSubResources(tenantId);
  await validateNoResidualData(tenantId);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- What if deletion fails on one service after others succeed?
- How would you automate periodic offboarding to ensure compliance and completeness?
